cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "TokWatt: an open, boundary-annotated database of AI inference energy"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Bahi"
    given-names: "Abderaouf"
    affiliation: "LIMA Laboratory"
    email: "a.bahi@univ-eltarf.dz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/tokwatt"
url: "https://USERNAME.github.io/tokwatt/"
abstract: >-
  TokWatt collects first-hand estimates of the energy used by AI inference
  (chat answers, reasoning, long-document queries, agentic tasks, image and
  video generation, classic ML tasks), records each with its measurement
  boundary and functional unit, and derives harmonized per-task reference
  values with reproducible rules. It also provides data-centre electricity
  indicators, country grid carbon intensities and everyday energy equivalents.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - energy consumption
  - inference
  - data centers
  - large language models
  - sustainability
  - carbon footprint
